a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:271:### 2.1 Positioning: body version 3, one profile\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:306:### 2.3 The frame rows (replacing draft §5.2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:698:image ids), `space`, `segment-of`, `register-pairs`, `correspondence`,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:862:1. **pc correspondence.** The stack emitter visits parse nodes in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1435:takes an **explicit logical-stream correspondence** from the fixture:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1461:explicit, injective logical-stream correspondence and a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1466:the same correspondence befor