{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '65,130p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '640,703p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '845,946p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '930,961p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc | sed -n '1470,1530p'\"","aggregated_output":"    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(defn- child-places\n    68\t  \"`[[coordinate child-address] ...]` of one row in grammar order: a `node`\n    69\t   slot's coordinate is its full-row position, a `nodes` child's is\n    70\t   `[position i]` (§2.1).\"\n    71\t  [row]\n    72\t  (mapcat (fn [[pos kind]]\n    73\t            (case kind\n    74\t              :node [[pos (nth row pos)]]\n    75\t              :nodes (map-indexed (fn [i c] [[pos i] c]) (nth row pos))\n    76\t              nil))\n    77\t          (slot-kinds (row-tag row))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- with-child\n    81\t  \"`row`'s body with the child at coordinate `coord` replaced by `address`.\"\n    82\t  [row coord address]\n    83\t  (let [body (subvec row 1)]\n    84\t    (if (vector? coord)\n    85\t      (let [[pos i] coord]\n    86\t        (assoc body (dec pos) (assoc (nth row pos) i address)))\n    87\t      (assoc body (dec coord) address))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn- reachable\n    91\t  \"Addresses reachable from `root` through `index`, first-encounter preorder\n    92\t   in grammar order. Assumes the index is closed and acyclic.\"\n    93\t  [index root]\n    94\t  (loop [stack (list root)\n    95\t         seen #{}\n    96\t         order []]\n    97\t    (if-let [a (first stack)]\n    98\t      (if (contains? seen a)\n    99\t        (recur (rest stack) seen order)\n   100\t        (recur (reduce conj (rest stack) (reverse (map second (child-places (get index a)))))\n   101\t               (conj seen a)\n   102\t               (conj order a)))\n   103\t      order)))\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\t(defn- packet-of\n   107\t  \"The self-contained tree packet `[root rows]` rooted at `root` (§1.2). Row\n   108\t   order is preorder, which is deterministic but carries no meaning.\"\n   109\t  [index root]\n   110\t  [root (mapv #(get index %) (reachable index root))])\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\t(defn tree-packet\n   114\t  \"Convert a projected row set `{:root id :rows {id row}}` (the shape\n   115\t   `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode` returns) to a tree packet `[root rows]`.\"\n   116\t  [{:keys [root rows]}]\n   117\t  (packet-of rows root))\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\t(defn packet->row-set\n   121\t  \"Convert a canonical tree packet to `{:root id :rows {id row}}`, the shape\n   122\t   the evaluator loaders take.\"\n   123\t  [[root rows]]\n   124\t  {:root root, :rows (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) rows)})\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn ast->packet\n   128\t  \"Project a map AST to its canonical tree packet.\"\n   129\t  [ast]\n   130\t  (tree-packet (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)))\n   640\t(defn- sequence-body\n   641\t  \"The reference `do` lowering: `(do a b c)` is `((fn [_] ((fn [_] c) b)) a)`;\n   642\t   one form is itself and none is the literal nil.\"\n   643\t  [trees]\n   644\t  (let [trees (vec trees)]\n   645\t    (doseq [t trees] (need-packet 'yin/sequence-body t))\n   646\t    (case (count trees)\n   647\t      0 (literal-packet nil)\n   648\t      1 (first trees)\n   649\t      (application-packet (lambda-packet ['_] (sequence-body (subvec trees 1)))\n   650\t                          [(first trees)]))))\n   651\t\n   652\t\n   653\t(defn- slot-of\n   654\t  [tree n]\n   655\t  (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/slot tree))\n   656\t        kinds (into {} (slot-kinds (row-tag row)))\n   657\t        index (packet-index tree)]\n   658\t    (when-not (and (integer? n) (contains? kinds n))\n   659\t      (throw-prelude \"yin/slot position names no grammar slot\"\n   660\t                     {:op 'yin/slot, :position n}))\n   661\t    (case (get kinds n)\n   662\t      :node (packet-of index (nth row n))\n   663\t      :nodes (mapv #(packet-of index %) (nth row n))\n   664\t      (nth row n))))\n   665\t\n   666\t\n   667\t(defn prelude\n   668\t  \"The closed body environment (§5.3): the pure standard primitives (no\n   669\t   `require`, no stream or FFI constructor) and the row-native constructors,\n   670\t   each consuming and returning self-contained tree packets. `gensym` is the\n   671\t   invocation-local `yin/gensym-sym`.\"\n   672\t  [gensym]\n   673\t  (merge\n   674\t    (dissoc vm/primitives 'require 'try-require 'bytes->str)\n   675\t    {'yin/tag (fn [tree] (row-tag (root-row (need-packet 'yin/tag tree)))),\n   676\t     'yin/slot slot-of,\n   677\t     'yin/literal literal-packet,\n   678\t     'yin/variable (fn [sym]\n   679\t                     (when-not (symbol? sym)\n   680\t                       (throw-prelude \"yin/variable expects a symbol\" {:op 'yin/variable}))\n   681\t                     (construct [:variable sym] [])),\n   682\t     'yin/lambda (fn [params body] (lambda-packet params (need-packet 'yin/lambda body))),\n   683\t     'yin/application (fn [operator operands]\n   684\t                        (need-packet 'yin/application operator)\n   685\t                        (doseq [o operands] (need-packet 'yin/application o))\n   686\t                        (application-packet operator (vec operands))),\n   687\t     'yin/if (fn [t c a]\n   688\t               (doseq [x [t c a]] (need-packet 'yin/if x))\n   689\t               (construct [:if (first t) (first c) (first a)] [t c a])),\n   690\t     'yin/sequence-body sequence-body,\n   691\t     'yin/make-lambda (fn [params-tree body]\n   692\t                        (let [row (root-row (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda params-tree))]\n   693\t                          (when-not (and (= :literal (row-tag row))\n   694\t                                         (vector? (nth row 2))\n   695\t                                         (every? symbol? (nth row 2)))\n   696\t                            (throw-prelude \"yin/make-lambda reads a literal parameter vector\"\n   697\t                                           {:op 'yin/make-lambda}))\n   698\t                          (lambda-packet (nth row 2) (need-packet 'yin/make-lambda body)))),\n   699\t     'yin/make-def (fn [name-tree value-tree]\n   700\t                     (application-packet (construct [:variable 'yin/def] [])\n   701\t                                         [(literal-packet (name-of name-tree))\n   702\t                                          (need-packet 'yin/make-def value-tree)])),\n   703\t     'yin/name-of name-of,\n   845\t        (if error\n   846\t          {:error (assoc error :macro macro-root)}\n   847\t          {:tree value})))))\n   848\t\n   849\t\n   850\t(def default-guards\n   851\t  {:max-depth 100,\n   852\t   :max-rows-per-expansion 10000,\n   853\t   :max-rows-per-batch nil,\n   854\t   :max-steps 100000})\n   855\t\n   856\t\n   857\t(defn invoke\n   858\t  \"Run `entry`, a macro-store value (`macro-entry`: a self-contained lambda\n   859\t   packet and its AST contract), on `operand-trees` and return its result\n   860\t   tree packet, unvalidated. The contract is verified first\n   861\t   (`:contract-missing`, `:contract-mismatch`, thrown). Gensyms use\n   862\t   `(:attempt ctx)` as the attempt counter. Throws `ex-info` carrying the\n   863\t   error data on an arity, guard, suspension, or body failure.\"\n   864\t  [entry operand-trees ctx]\n   865\t  (let [ctx (update ctx :guards #(merge default-guards %))\n   866\t        {:keys [tree error]} (invoke* entry (vec operand-trees) ctx\n   867\t                                      (:attempt ctx))]\n   868\t    (when error\n   869\t      (throw (ex-info \"Macro invocation failed\" error)))\n   870\t    tree))\n   871\t\n   872\t\n   873\t;; =============================================================================\n   874\t;; Tail marking and lowering (§6, §3.2 steps 6-7)\n   875\t;; =============================================================================\n   876\t\n   877\t(defn- retail\n   878\t  \"Recompute every `tail?` slot below `root`, in context `tail?`, over a\n   879\t   working index; `[index' root']`. Tail-ness is contextual, so one shared\n   880\t   row in two contexts becomes two rows.\"\n   881\t  [index root]\n   882\t  (let [memo (volatile! {})]\n   883\t    (letfn [(go\n   884\t              [index a tail?]\n   885\t              (if-let [hit (get @memo [a tail?])]\n   886\t                [index hit]\n   887\t                (let [row (get index a)\n   888\t                      tag (row-tag row)\n   889\t                      ctxs (case tag\n   890\t                             :lambda [true]\n   891\t                             :if [false tail? tail?]\n   892\t                             (repeat false))\n   893\t                      [index children']\n   894\t                      (reduce (fn [[index acc] [[_ c] t]]\n   895\t                                (let [[index c'] (go index c t)]\n   896\t                                  [index (conj acc c')]))\n   897\t                              [index []]\n   898\t                              (map vector (child-places row) ctxs))\n   899\t                      [index a'] (rebuild-row index row children')\n   900\t                      [index a'] (if (and (= :application tag)\n   901\t                                          (not= tail? (nth (get index a') 4)))\n   902\t                                   (intern-body index (assoc (subvec (get index a') 1) 3 tail?))\n   903\t                                   [index a'])]\n   904\t                  (vswap! memo assoc [a tail?] a')\n   905\t                  [index a'])))]\n   906\t      (go index root true))))\n   907\t\n   908\t\n   909\t(defn mark-tail\n   910\t  \"Recompute all observable tail slots of a tree packet, setting and\n   911\t   clearing marks (§6): the root is in tail context, an `:if` test is\n   912\t   non-tail and its branches inherit, application operators and operands are\n   913\t   non-tail, a lambda body is tail, and every other child is non-tail.\"\n   914\t  [packet]\n   915\t  (let [[index root] (retail (packet-index packet) (first packet))]\n   916\t    (packet-of index root)))\n   917\t\n   918\t\n   919\t(defn- lower-standins\n   920\t  \"Replace every stand-in by the canonical literal of its name.\"\n   921\t  [index root]\n   922\t  (let [memo (volatile! {})]\n   923\t    (letfn [(go\n   924\t              [index a]\n   925\t              (if-let [hit (get @memo a)]\n   926\t                [index hit]\n   927\t                (let [row (get index a)\n   928\t                      [index a']\n   929\t                      (if (= standin-tag (row-tag row))\n   930\t                        (intern-body index [:literal (nth row 2)])\n   931\t                        (let [[index children']\n   932\t                              (reduce (fn [[index acc] [_ c]]\n   933\t                                        (let [[index c'] (go index c)]\n   934\t                                          [index (conj acc c')]))\n   935\t                                      [index []]\n   936\t                                      (child-places row))]\n   937\t                          (rebuild-row index row children')))]\n   938\t                  (vswap! memo assoc a a')\n   939\t                  [index a'])))]\n   940\t      (go index root))))\n   941\t\n   942\t\n   943\t;; =============================================================================\n   944\t;; Harvest and post-harvest (§3.2 steps 2, 3, 5; §3.5)\n   945\t;; =============================================================================\n   946\t\n   930\t                   true\n   931\t                   (map? x) (and (every? machine-data? (keys x))\n   932\t                                 (every? machine-data? (vals x)))\n   933\t                   (coll? x) (every? machine-data? x)\n   934\t                   :else false)\n   935\t             (machine-data? (meta x))))))\n   936\t\n   937\t\n   938\t(defn occurrence-origin?\n   939\t  \"True when `origin` has one of §2.5's portable ruled shapes. `nil` is not\n   940\t   an occurrence; it is accepted separately by the legacy bare-row lane.\n   941\t\n   942\t   A source origin is `[:source medium batch-token member-index]`. Medium and\n   943\t   token are opaque non-nil plain data supplied by the admitting composition,\n   944\t   and the member index is a non-negative integer. An expansion origin names\n   945\t   the portable content address of its expansion record.\"\n   946\t  [origin]\n   947\t  (and (vector? origin)\n   948\t       (case (first origin)\n   949\t         :source (and (= 4 (count origin))\n   950\t                      (some? (nth origin 1))\n   951\t                      (plain-data? (nth origin 1))\n   952\t                      (some? (nth origin 2))\n   953\t                      (plain-data? (nth origin 2))\n   954\t                      (integer? (nth origin 3))\n   955\t                      (not (neg? (nth origin 3))))\n   956\t         :expansion (and (= 2 (count origin))\n   957\t                         (jing/segment-address? (nth origin 1)))\n   958\t         false)))\n   959\t\n   960\t\n   961\t(defn source-origin\n  1470\t   log writer, with nothing staged.\"\n  1471\t  ([ctx out] (make-expander ctx out nil))\n  1472\t  ([ctx out log]\n  1473\t   {:ctx ctx, :out out, :out-staged nil, :log log, :log-staged nil,\n  1474\t    :forwarded 0, :errors []}))\n  1475\t\n  1476\t\n  1477\t(defn ready?\n  1478\t  \"Ready only when both staged slots are empty.\"\n  1479\t  [expander]\n  1480\t  (and (nil? (:out-staged expander)) (nil? (:log-staged expander))))\n  1481\t\n  1482\t\n  1483\t(defn call-site-table\n  1484\t  \"The C1 side table the consumer `expander` holds for the occurrence\n  1485\t   the executed tree packet `tree` names — `origin` being the admission\n  1486\t   origin the table was stored under (§2.1: an application site is\n  1487\t   K = [origin root-address path]; the table's key is the admission\n  1488\t   origin beside the root address, while each row's own origin names\n  1489\t   that occurrence's admission or generating expansion record) — or nil when\n  1490\t   that occurrence made no C1 claim. Two expansions can produce the\n  1491\t   SAME final root from different admissions; keying by the full\n  1492\t   occurrence identity keeps their tables distinct, so resolving by the\n  1493\t   origin+root pair at hand never answers another execution's table,\n  1494\t   however many loads have run since, and an unclaimed load of a root\n  1495\t   previously loaded under a claim retrieves no stale table.\"\n  1496\t  [expander tree origin]\n  1497\t  (get (:call-site-tables expander) [origin (first tree)]))\n  1498\t\n  1499\t\n  1500\t(defn load\n  1501\t  \"Expand one observed batch once: keep the returned context, stage the\n  1502\t   tree only on success, stage the log when a log writer exists, and\n  1503\t   accumulate the error of a failed expansion. Expansion failure is\n  1504\t   data, so the cursor advances past it. A successful expansion's C1\n  1505\t   side table (the batch result's `:frontend-metadata`, present only\n  1506\t   when the selected member itself claimed coverage) is retained on the\n  1507\t   consumer under the occurrence identity of the staged tree — its\n  1508\t   admission origin beside its final root address (`call-site-tables`,\n  1509\t   resolved by `call-site-table`) — so the composition that drives this\n  1510\t   expander — the REPL's session — holds every executed occurrence's\n  1511\t   coverage beside the expander that produced it, each load's table\n  1512\t   surviving the next, even when two loads land on the same root.\"\n  1513\t  [expander batch]\n  1514\t  (let [{:keys [status tree log error ctx frontend-metadata\n  1515\t                call-site-origin]}\n  1516\t        (expand-batch batch (:ctx expander))]\n  1517\t    (cond-> (assoc expander :ctx ctx)\n  1518\t      (= :ok status) (assoc :out-staged tree)\n  1519\t      (and (= :ok status) frontend-metadata)\n  1520\t      (assoc-in [:call-site-tables [call-site-origin (first tree)]]\n  1521\t                frontend-metadata)\n  1522\t      (:log expander) (assoc :log-staged log)\n  1523\t      (= :error status) (update :errors conj error))))\n  1524\t\n  1525\t\n  1526\t(defn- flush-slot\n  1527\t  [expander writer-key slot-key on-ok]\n  1528\t  (if-let [payload (get expander slot-key)]\n  1529\t    (let [outcome (:dao.stream/outcome (stream/append! (get expander writer-key) payload))]\n  1530\t      (case outcome\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"I found two blocking residuals. A nested macro that passes through an admitted operand assigns it the enclosing generated call’s origin. The default publication counter also restarts at zero in each process under the same fixed medium, so it can repeat admission identities. The corrected `unless` fixture is valid; it doesn’t exercise the nested case.\n"}}
