{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc | sed -n '190,230p'; nl -ba test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '270,393p'; nl -ba test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | sed -n '715,785p'; rg -n 'defn- kernel-stamp-sites|call-site-key|yang/call-site' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; nl -ba docs/design/datom.world.md | sed -n '23,38p'\"","aggregated_output":"   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(declare walk-module)\n   193\t\n   194\t\n   195\t(defn- walk-call-sites\n   196\t  \"Step 4b: the C1 side table and its reverse record the manifest\n   197\t   references (`:yin.module/call-sites`, `yin.vm.linker.publish`), read\n   198\t   and held to their own shape — the table is a vector of frontend-\n   199\t   metadata rows, the record is version 1, names the manifest's own\n   200\t   tree, and points at the referenced table. The origin is left to the\n   201\t   retriever, which recomputes it from the tree.\"\n   202\t  [st manifest path]\n   203\t  (if-some [call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\n   204\t    (let [[st table] (read-blob st (:table call-sites) :call-site path)]\n   205\t      (if (:stop st)\n   206\t        st\n   207\t        (let [[st record] (read-blob st (:record call-sites) :call-site path)]\n   208\t          (cond\n   209\t            (:stop st) st\n   210\t\n   211\t            (not (vector? table))\n   212\t            (stop st (invalid (:table call-sites) :call-site path\n   213\t                              :call-site-defect {:code :table-shape}))\n   214\t\n   215\t            (not= {:yang.call-site/version 1\n   216\t                   :yang.call-site/root (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n   217\t                   :yang.call-site/table (:table call-sites)}\n   218\t                  (select-keys record\n   219\t                               [:yang.call-site/version\n   220\t                                :yang.call-site/root\n   221\t                                :yang.call-site/table]))\n   222\t            (stop st (invalid (:record call-sites) :call-site path\n   223\t                              :call-site-defect {:code :record-shape}))\n   224\t\n   225\t            :else st))))\n   226\t    st))\n   227\t\n   228\t\n   229\t(defn- walk-requires\n   230\t  \"Step 5: list every pin with derived eagerness, then descend only into\n   270\t   `encoder/program-batch` (what `yin.repl`'s eval-program appends to\n   271\t   program-in) into the row-native expander, seeded as the REPL seeds\n   272\t   its session expander — the standard forms folded through a throwaway\n   273\t   context, then a fresh session context holding that store. Answers\n   274\t   `{:ctx ctx :result expansion}`, where `ctx` is the admitting\n   275\t   context (its `:t` is the batch's source coordinate).\"\n   276\t  [ast]\n   277\t  (let [store (macro/seed-store\n   278\t                (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n   279\t                                 :source-medium :callsite-test/standard-forms})\n   280\t                [macro/stdlib-forms])\n   281\t        ctx (macro/make-ctx {:token \"callsite-test\"\n   282\t                             :source-medium :program-in\n   283\t                             :store store})]\n   284\t    {:ctx ctx\n   285\t     :result (macro/expand-batch (encoder/program-batch ast) ctx)}))\n   286\t\n   287\t\n   288\t(deftest post-expansion-coverage-test\n   289\t  (testing \"the marker set covers the tree the REPL pipeline actually executes\"\n   290\t    (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n   291\t                '[(defmacro unless [c a b] (yin/if c b a))\n   292\t                  (unless false (+ 1 2) 0)])\n   293\t          {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n   294\t          {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n   295\t          ;; the row set the evaluator loaders consume from program-out\n   296\t          final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n   297\t          ;; the ADMISSION origin of this expansion — the table's key\n   298\t          ;; coordinate, never a blanket stamp on the rows (design §2.1:\n   299\t          ;; generated post-expansion syntax must not be mislabeled as\n   300\t          ;; original source)\n   301\t          admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n   302\t          input-tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n   303\t          input-tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast input-tree admission)\n   304\t          ;; the expansion record addresses the log actually holds: the\n   305\t          ;; only legitimate `[:expansion a]` origins are these\n   306\t          event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n   307\t          origins (row-origins frontend-metadata)]\n   308\t      (is (= :ok status))\n   309\t      (testing \"expansion changed the tree: the `(unless …)` call expanded\"\n   310\t        (is (not= (:root input-tree) (:root final))))\n   311\t      (testing \"the changed root carries no fabricated expansion origin\n   312\t                (design §2.1: post-expansion names the pipeline\n   313\t                boundary, not proof that a generating event occurred)\"\n   314\t        (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n   315\t        (is (every? (fn [o]\n   316\t                      (or (= o admission)\n   317\t                          (and (expansion-origin? o)\n   318\t                               (contains? event-addrs (second o)))))\n   319\t                    origins)\n   320\t            \"every origin is the admission's source origin or names a\n   321\t             recorded expansion event — nothing fabricated\")\n   322\t        ;; the `(unless …)` output's generated node is an `:if`, not an\n   323\t        ;; application, and its `(+ 1 2)` operand is the admitted\n   324\t        ;; operand passed through — so every APPLICATION here is\n   325\t        ;; retained admitted syntax and genuinely keeps the source\n   326\t        ;; origin; the source origin is not a blanket stamp, it is the\n   327\t        ;; real provenance of each marked occurrence\n   328\t        (is (= #{admission} origins)\n   329\t            \"no generating event produced an application here, so every\n   330\t             marked occurrence is admitted\"))\n   331\t      (testing \"the retained table covers exactly the executed tree\"\n   332\t        (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n   333\t        (is (every? (fn [[_ r _ _ _]] (= (:root final) r))\n   334\t                    frontend-metadata))\n   335\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   336\t                     final frontend-metadata admission\n   337\t                     {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true}))))\n   338\t      (testing \"the frontend's pre-expansion markers name a tree that no longer exists\"\n   339\t        (is (= :yang/call-site-nonexistent-path\n   340\t               (failure-rule\n   341\t                 #(yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   342\t                    final (:frontend-metadata input-tables) admission))))))\n   343\t    (testing \"a generating expansion marks its generated applications\n   344\t              with the recorded expansion record's origin (design §2.1,\n   345\t              §2.3: the correspondence is explicit, never fabricated)\"\n   346\t      (let [ast (yang/compile-program\n   347\t                  '[(defmacro make-call [x]\n   348\t                      (yin/application (yin/variable 'f) [x]))\n   349\t                    (defn f [y] (+ y 1))\n   350\t                    (make-call 2)])\n   351\t            {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n   352\t            {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata log]} result\n   353\t            final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n   354\t            admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]\n   355\t            event-addrs (into #{} (map first) (nth log 1))\n   356\t            origins (row-origins frontend-metadata)\n   357\t            generated (into #{}\n   358\t                            (comp (filter #(expansion-origin? (first %)))\n   359\t                                  (map #(vec (take 3 %))))\n   360\t                            frontend-metadata)]\n   361\t        (is (= :ok status))\n   362\t        (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n   363\t        (is (seq generated)\n   364\t            \"the macro generated an application, and it is marked\")\n   365\t        (is (contains? origins admission)\n   366\t            \"the admitted applications keep the source origin\")\n   367\t        (is (every? (fn [[o _ _]] (contains? event-addrs (second o))) generated)\n   368\t            \"each generated occurrence names a recorded expansion event\")\n   369\t        (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n   370\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   371\t                     final frontend-metadata admission\n   372\t                     {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true})))))\n   373\t    (testing \"a no-op expansion retains the admitted source origin\"\n   374\t      ;; no macro call at all: the pipeline boundary alone (tail\n   375\t      ;; marking) changes the root without a generating event, so the\n   376\t      ;; final rows legitimately keep the admission's source origin\n   377\t      (let [ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (+ x 1)) (f 2)])\n   378\t            {:keys [ctx result]} (expand-like-the-repl ast)\n   379\t            {:keys [status tree frontend-metadata]} result\n   380\t            final (macro/packet->row-set tree)\n   381\t            admission [:source :program-in (:t ctx) 0]]\n   382\t        (is (= :ok status))\n   383\t        (is (seq frontend-metadata))\n   384\t        (is (= #{admission} (row-origins frontend-metadata))\n   385\t            \"no generating event occurred, so the source origin remains\n   386\t             valid for every occurrence (design §2.1)\")\n   387\t        (is (= (occurrence-pairs final) (marked-pairs frontend-metadata)))\n   388\t        (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   389\t                     final frontend-metadata admission\n   390\t                     {:declared? true :per-occurrence-origins? true}))))))\n   391\t  (testing \"the expander consumer the REPL threads retains the executed tree's table\"\n   392\t    (let [store (macro/seed-store\n   393\t                  (macro/make-ctx {:token :callsite-test/standard-forms\n   715\t            (is (some? rows)\n   716\t                \"the markers are retrievable from the published module\")\n   717\t            (is (pos? (count rows)))\n   718\t            (is (= (eligible-under tree origin) (marked rows)))\n   719\t            (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   720\t                         tree rows origin {:declared? true}))))))))\n   721\t  (testing \"two publications of identical trees are two admissions\n   722\t            (design §2.1), and a retrieval replays the one recorded\n   723\t            admission it names\"\n   724\t    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   725\t          ast (yang/compile-program '[(defn f [x] (inc x)) (f 2)])\n   726\t          spec {:name 'twin-admissions\n   727\t                :ast ast\n   728\t                :exports #{'f}\n   729\t                :requires {}\n   730\t                :primitives {'inc {:yin.k/profile :yin.k/pure\n   731\t                                   :yin.k/effects #{}}}}\n   732\t          first-result (publish/publish-module! store spec)\n   733\t          second-result (publish/publish-module! store spec)\n   734\t          first-address (:address first-result)\n   735\t          second-address (:address second-result)]\n   736\t      (is (some? first-address))\n   737\t      (is (some? second-address))\n   738\t      (is (not= first-address second-address)\n   739\t          \"the manifests differ, because each references its own table\")\n   740\t      (testing \"identical content, distinct admission identities\"\n   741\t        (is (= (get-in first-result [:call-sites :root])\n   742\t               (get-in second-result [:call-sites :root]))\n   743\t            \"the published trees are content-identical\")\n   744\t        (is (not= (get-in first-result [:call-sites :origin])\n   745\t                  (get-in second-result [:call-sites :origin]))\n   746\t            \"separately admitted identical sources have different origins\"))\n   747\t      (testing \"retrieval reads each record's recorded admission\"\n   748\t        (doseq [[label result address]\n   749\t                [[\"first\" first-result first-address]\n   750\t                 [\"second\" second-result second-address]]]\n   751\t          (let [retrieved (publish/published-call-site-table store address)]\n   752\t            (is (some? retrieved) (str label \" table retrieves\"))\n   753\t            (is (= (get-in result [:call-sites :origin]) (:origin retrieved))\n   754\t                (str label \" retrieval answers the recorded admission, \"\n   755\t                     \"never a reconstructed one\"))\n   756\t            (is (= (:origin retrieved)\n   757\t                   (:origin (publish/published-call-site-table store address)))\n   758\t                (str label \" replaying the retrieval replays the same \"\n   759\t                     \"recorded admission\")))\n   760\t          (let [{:keys [tree origin rows]}\n   761\t                (publish/published-call-site-table store address)]\n   762\t            (is (= (eligible-under tree origin) (marked rows)))\n   763\t            (is (true? (yang/validate-call-site-coverage!\n   764\t                         tree rows origin {:declared? true}))))))\n   765\t      (testing \"a composition may pin the admission identity explicitly\"\n   766\t        (let [pinned (publish/publish-module!\n   767\t                       store spec\n   768\t                       {:yin.link.publish/admission \"pinned-admission\"})]\n   769\t          (is (some? (:address pinned)))\n   770\t          (is (= [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish\n   771\t                  \"pinned-admission\" 0]\n   772\t                 (get-in pinned [:call-sites :origin]))\n   773\t              \"the pinned token is the admission identity, persisted in\n   774\t               the record and retrieved from it\")\n   775\t          (is (= [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish\n   776\t                  \"pinned-admission\" 0]\n   777\t                 (:origin (publish/published-call-site-table\n   778\t                            store (:address pinned)))))))))\n   779\t  (testing \"an unannotated module publishes no table and claims none\"\n   780\t    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n   781\t          plain (publish/publish-module!\n   782\t                  store {:name 'plain\n   783\t                         :ast {:type :application\n   784\t                               :operator {:type :variable :name 'yin/def}\n   785\t                               :operands [{:type :literal :value 'f}\n2192:(defn- kernel-stamp-sites\n    23\t\n    24\t## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n    25\t\n    26\t- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n    27\t- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n    28\t- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n    29\t- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n    30\t- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n    31\t- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n    32\t- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n    33\t\n    34\t## Tuples and Datoms\n    35\t\n    36\tTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\n    37\tA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\n    38\tSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
